## 🔍 4. RE-ENGINEERING DATA SPECIFICATIONS (24-Feature Matrix)
To successfully pass the strict structural requirements of the LightGBM inference model, incoming payloads must be strictly mapped into the following data matrix schema before entering `predict_proba`:

| No. | Feature Name | Data Type | Business Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1-6 | `financial_apps_installed`, ... | `float64` | Behavioral metrics for app usage and transactions |
| 7 | `existing_debt_amount` | `float64` | Base system debt value (converted into USD) |
| 8-10 | `income_bracket_1.0` -> `3.0` | `float64` | One-Hot encoded income bracket dummy columns |
| 11-13 | `employment_type_1.0` -> `3.0` | `float64` | One-Hot encoded employment type dummy columns |
| 14-16 | `education_level_1.0` -> `3.0` | `float64` | One-Hot encoded education level dummy columns |
| 17-19 | `cluster_id_0.0` -> `2.0` | `float64` | One-Hot encoded behavioral cluster dummy columns |
| 20-23 | `income_bracket`, `employment_type`, ...| `float64` | Raw numerical features serving decision tree splits |

